    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h3>Reproducible, not hand-built</h3>
        <p>
          If an environment cannot be rebuilt from source control, it is a
          liability. Everything I build is defined as code, validated in CI and
          documented for whoever inherits it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Straight answers</h3>
        <p>
          Sometimes the right advice is that a migration is not worth it, or that
          AI will not help with the problem you have. You will get that view
          early, not after the invoice.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Security as a default</h3>
        <p>
          Hardening, identity and least privilege designed in from the start.
          Controls engineers route around are worse than none at all.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Evidence over adjectives</h3>
        <p>
          Working reference implementations are published publicly so you can
          inspect the standard of work before you commit to anything.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
